\DOC constructors_distinct_net

\TYPE {constructors_distinct_net : (int * conv) net ref}

\SYNOPSIS
Net of conversions proving distinctness of constructors of inductive types.

\DESCRIBE
This net contains, for each constructor {C} of each inductive type defined so
far that has at least two constructors, an entry with a pattern
{`C x1 ... xn = y`} and a conversion proving
{|- C s1 ... sn = D t1 ... tm <=> F} for the other constructors {D} of the same
type, as produced by {constructors_distinct_convs}. It covers the types
defined by {define_type} as well as {bool}, {num}, {list}, {option} and {sum}.
The net is extended automatically by {extend_rectype_net}, which is called by
{define_type}, and it is used by {CONSTRUCTORS_DISTINCT_CONV}. The same entries
are also in {basic_rectype_net}.

\FAILURE
Not applicable.

\EXAMPLE
The conversion {CONSTRUCTORS_DISTINCT_CONV} simply rewrites with this net:
{
  # REWRITES_CONV (!constructors_distinct_net) `SOME (x:num) = NONE`;;
  val it : thm = |- SOME x = NONE <=> F
}

\SEEALSO
basic_rectype_net, CONSTRUCTORS_DISTINCT_CONV, constructors_distinct_convs,
define_type, extend_rectype_net, REWRITES_CONV.

\ENDDOC
